{"name":"Toxic Boyfriend","hex":"#ccff11","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toxic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a chemical nature that is harmful to health or lethal if consumed or otherwise entering into the body in sufficient quantities.","Appearing grossly unwell; characterised by serious, potentially life-threatening compromise in the respiratory, circulatory or other body systems."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toxic"},{"term":"boyfriend","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male partner in an unmarried romantic relationship.","A male friend."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be a boyfriend to (someone).","To have (someone) as a boyfriend."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boyfriend"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toxicity","blocks":[{"text":"Toxicity is the degree to which a chemical substance or a particular mixture of substances can damage an organism. Toxicity can refer to the effect on a whole organism, such as an animal, bacterium, or plant, as well as the effect on a substructure of the organism, such as a cell (cytotoxicity) or an organ such as the liver (hepatotoxicity). Sometimes the word is more or less synonymous with poisoning in everyday usage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Skull_and_Crossbones.svg/330px-Skull_and_Crossbones.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toxicity"},{"title":"Boyfriend","blocks":[{"text":"A boyfriend is a man who is a friend or acquaintance to the speaker, often specifying a regular male companion with whom a person is platonically, romantically or sexually involved."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boyfriend"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-P0310-0025%2C_Berlin%2C_Stra%C3%9Fenszene.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-P0310-0025%2C_Berlin%2C_Str